{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["For I am gracious — even though by strict law he has the right to hold the pledge and is not obligated to return it, and this would be beyond the line of justice, and I would have had no obligation to hear his outcry — were it not that I am compassionate and gracious. But above, in the case of the widow and the orphan — כי אם צעק יצעק אלי שמע אשמע צעקתו is written. Since by strict law the Holy One, blessed be He, hears their outcry, therefore it is not written there 'for I am gracious.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:41.090937372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}